  "name": "connect-cdc-postgres",
  "description": "Streams change data capture from PostgreSQL into Redpanda or Kafka using Redpanda Connect's postgres_cdc input, which reads the WAL through logical replication (pgoutput). Use when configuring postgres_cdc (formerly pg_stream), setting up wal_level=logical, replication slots, and publications, enabling an initial snapshot before streaming, or troubleshooting slot growth and WAL accumulation. Also covers Redpanda Enterprise destination features such as Iceberg Topics, Tiered Storage, and server-side Schema ID Validation, since postgres_cdc itself requires a Redpanda Enterprise license.",
